    },
    {
      "id": "claim_07f47e2583ed4e91b2e59fafd413b09a",
      "statement": "TypeSafeConfig defines the TypeSafeClient bean itself (instead of the TypeSafe starter's auto-configuration) so a blank API key never crashes startup; it builds a Jev-only Reactor Netty request factory (connect 5s, read = spring.ai.typesafe.timeout) on a clone() of the auto-configured RestClient.Builder, and sets baseUrl explicitly so the SDK never falls back to its own TYPESAFE_* environment variables.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/TypeSafeConfig.java#L23-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fde25f643fd3b97ff438f82f3b7a177d8dd3ef273ab9714b2b879e52f27a242b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_312b5df398154974aae79870f593b55b",
      "statement": "Both RaindropApiClientImpl and JevApiClientImpl put @CircuitBreaker(name=\"...\") and @Retry(name=\"...\") on the API-client bean rather than the service layer, so business validation (not-configured/disabled checks) runs outside the breaker and only the real HTTP/SDK call is wrapped; self-invocation would bypass the AOP proxy, which is why the annotated methods live on a bean the service calls into.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/JevApiClientImpl.java#L34-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4dea63b6d8809da18ee6d6686a9ac891fb002d8dbeaece66862563df247e8492:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropApiClientImpl.java#L26-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8332019c14e4bbb7bf25791e6ddb587388dbd6ef13892bef84ba7a2576732d59:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40aeb34d3cb64c3ebcd7d512a576f679",
      "statement": "The Resilience4j annotations only take effect because spring-boot-starter-aspectj is on the classpath; execution order is set globally via resilience4j.circuitbreaker.circuit-breaker-aspect-order: 1 and resilience4j.retry.retry-aspect-order: 2 (lower = outer) so the breaker wraps the retry and records one outcome per logical call rather than per retry attempt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L159-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d0f0bb55f483bcbec973740f2ac49b5e091a9dd6ba07fd14118983c5546e27a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b33ea51354784df6b980bdea645dd951",
      "statement": "Each client's not-configured exception (RaindropNotConfiguredException, JevNotConfiguredException) is listed under ignore-exceptions for both its circuit-breaker and retry instances so a missing token/key never opens the breaker or burns a retry attempt; RaindropApiClientImpl uses a fallbackMethod that re-throws RaindropNotConfiguredException as-is and wraps other failures as IllegalStateException (409), while JevApiClientImpl has no fallback and lets typed TypeSafe exceptions and CallNotPermittedException propagate unchanged.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L160-L160",
